     "description": "Primarily celebrated for his goal-scoring prowess rather than his penalty-killing abilities, Brett Hull showcased his versatility in the clinching Game 6 of the Western Conference Quarterfinals against the Vancouver Canucks by netting the first of his three goals while shorthanded. His heroics that game were part of an incredible 10-goal performance during the 2002 Stanley Cup Playoffs, leading all players as he helped secure a Stanley Cup championship. Over his illustrious 19-season career, Hull scored 741 goals, ranking fifth all-time in NHL history.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
